{
  "summary": "The change adds guards against duplicate-key dictionary inserts in TypeCollector.GetObjectInfo and adds tests for SuppressSourceGeneration = true validation, but it inverts the mixed-key-detection condition at TypeCollector.cs lines 1005 and 1145. On head this crashes the analyzer (AD0001/NullReferenceException) on mixed int/string keys, emits false MsgPack005 diagnostics and drops members 2+ from generated formatters for every multi-key type, producing 34 new full-suite failures. The duplicate-key crash is fixed, but the mixed-key crash from base is not resolved and a broad regression is introduced; build passes and fail-without-fix was not run. Overall: blocker, do not merge until the condition is reverted and tests re-run.",
  "requirement_verdicts": [
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-F1",
      "verdict": "met",
      "confidence_basis": "All three F1-listed tests pass on head: missing-[Key] (MsgPack004), non-MessagePackObject member type (MsgPack003), and AllowPrivate required (MsgPack015) are all reported for suppressed types. The mixed-key-kind example named in F1's text is exercised under N1 and crashes there.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MemberWithoutKeyIsReported", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MemberTypeMustBeMessagePackObjectIsReported", "outcome": "passed"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.AllowPrivateRequiredIsReported", "outcome": "passed"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-F2",
      "verdict": "not_met",
      "confidence_basis": "Its covering test expects zero diagnostics for a suppressed type, but head reports a false MsgPack005 mixed-key diagnostic for Prop1, so the no-extra-diagnostics requirement is not demonstrated (the failure is the same inverted condition bug, not an F2-category diagnostic).",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.SourceGenerationOnlyDiagnosticsAreNotReportedWhenSuppressed", "outcome": "failed"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1005, "rev": "head", "quote": "if ((isIntKey && stringKey == null) || (!isIntKey && intKey == null))"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-N1",
      "verdict": "not_met",
      "confidence_basis": "MixedKeyKindsAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure crashes with AD0001 instead of reporting MsgPack005, and tests.full_suite fails with 34 new failures, so the analyzer/generator still crashes on invalid contracts in suppressed types.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MixedKeyKindsAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "failed"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1005, "rev": "head", "quote": "if ((isIntKey && stringKey == null) || (!isIntKey && intKey == null))"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1005, "rev": "base", "quote": "if ((isIntKey && intKey == null) || (!isIntKey && stringKey == null))"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "req": "REQ-2234-N2",
      "verdict": "not_met",
      "confidence_basis": "tests.fail_without_fix was not run, so it is unconfirmed that the new tests fail without the fix, and tests.full_suite has 34 regressions not present on base, violating the no-regression clause.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "F1",
      "title": "Mixed-key detection condition inverted; analyzer crashes on mixed int/string keys",
      "severity": "blocker",
      "category": "correctness",
      "claim": "TypeCollector.cs lines 1005 and 1145 use `(isIntKey && stringKey == null) || (!isIntKey && intKey == null)`, the inverse of the base condition. For a mixed type (int key then string key) no diagnostic is emitted and execution falls through to `intKey!.Value`/member.IntKey with a null key, throwing NullReferenceException (reported as analyzer crash AD0001). Base had the same crash at the unguarded `intMembers.Add`, so the change does not resolve the mixed-key crash from issue #2234.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1005, "rev": "head", "quote": "if ((isIntKey && stringKey == null) || (!isIntKey && intKey == null))"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1008, "rev": "head", "quote": "continue; // The key kind does not match the other members; the diagnostic is reported, so skip this member."},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1005, "rev": "base", "quote": "if ((isIntKey && intKey == null) || (!isIntKey && stringKey == null))"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.MixedKeyKindsAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailure", "outcome": "failed"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Restore the base condition `(isIntKey && intKey == null) || (!isIntKey && stringKey == null)` at both sites; keep the `continue` and the `ContainsKey` guards."
    },
    {
      "id": "F2",
      "title": "Same inverted condition reports false MsgPack005 and drops members 2+ from generated output",
      "severity": "blocker",
      "category": "correctness",
      "claim": "For any type with two or more same-kind keys, the second and later members satisfy `stringKey == null` (int keys) or `intKey == null` (string keys), so the condition falsely reports DoNotMixStringAndIntKeys (MsgPack005) and the `continue` skips the `intMembers.Add`/`stringMembers.Add`. Generated formatters omit members after the first, and analyzer tests see spurious MsgPack005 diagnostics.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1005, "rev": "head", "quote": "if ((isIntKey && stringKey == null) || (!isIntKey && intKey == null))"},
        {"kind": "code", "file": "src/MessagePack.SourceGenerator/CodeAnalysis/TypeCollector.cs", "line": 1025, "rev": "head", "quote": "intMembers.Add(member.IntKey, (member, item.Type));"},
        {"kind": "test", "name": "SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.SourceGenerationOnlyDiagnosticsAreNotReportedWhenSuppressed", "outcome": "failed"},
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Restore the base condition `(isIntKey && intKey == null) || (!isIntKey && stringKey == null)` at both sites; keep the `continue` and the `ContainsKey` guards."
    },
    {
      "id": "F3",
      "title": "Full-suite regressions; fail-without-fix not run",
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "tests",
      "claim": "tests.full_suite fails with 34 newly failing tests (0 also failing on base), including MsgPack00xAnalyzerTests false MsgPack005 diagnostics and GenerationTests/GenericsFormatterTests source-output mismatches, violating N2's no-regression clause. tests.fail_without_fix was not run, so coverage-without-fix is unconfirmed.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "check", "id": "tests.full_suite", "status": "fail"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Revert the condition flip, re-run fail-without-fix and the full suite, and require zero new failures before merge."
    },
    {
      "id": "F4",
      "title": "Test-file hygiene issues",
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "tests",
      "claim": "DuplicateKeysAreReportedWithoutAnalyzerFailureForGeneratedTypes tests a non-suppressed `[MessagePackObject]` type but lives in the suppressed-type analyzer test file, and the REQ-2234-F1 test list duplicates MemberWithoutKeyIsReported while omitting the duplicate/mixed-key tests.",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "code", "file": "tests/MessagePack.SourceGenerator.Tests/SuppressSourceGenerationAnalyzerTests.cs", "line": 150, "rev": "head", "quote": "[MessagePackObject]"}
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Move the non-suppressed duplicate-key test out of the suppressed analyzer test file and correct the REQ-2234-F1 test list."
    }
  ],
  "refusals": [
    {
      "topic": "Root-cause confirmation on base / whether tests fail without the fix",
      "reason": "tests.fail_without_fix was not run for this revision, so I cannot confirm the new tests fail without the fix or that the change resolves the original #2234 crash on base.",
      "who_should_decide": "area owner / decision engine",
      "req": "REQ-2234-N2",
      "blocking": false
    },
    {
      "topic": "Performance impact of the change",
      "reason": "No performance benchmarks or timing data were provided; the change's effect on analyzer/generator speed is unassessed.",
      "who_should_decide": "performance reviewer or area owner",
      "blocking": false
    }
  ],
  "refutations": []
}
